==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|incumbrance}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|encombraunce}}, from {{der|en|fro|encombrance}}, from {{m|fro|encombrer}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# Something that [[encumber]]s; a [[burden]] that must be [[carried]].
#* {{RQ:Grey Riders|8}}
#*: Some consideration was necessary to decide whether or not to leave his rifle there. On the return, carrying the girl and a pack, it would be added '''encumbrance'''{{...|; and after debating the matter he left the rifle leaning against the bench.}}
# {{lb|en|legal}} An [[interest]], [[right]], [[burden]], or [[liability]] attached to a [[title]] of [[land]], such as a [[lien]] or [[mortgage]].
# {{lb|en|legal}} One who is [[dependent]] on another.
#: ''a widow without '''encumbrances''', i.e. without children''

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|encumberment}}

